From: FingerBrowser
Subject: [PATCH 0011] UA/Client Hints and WebGPU identity consistency

Stop blanking high-entropy Client Hints when a custom UA is set under a
FingerBrowser profile; complete the Client Hints brand list with the product
brand a Chrome UA implies; and spoof the WebGPU adapter identity so it names
the same GPU as WebGL. All three remove same-page contradictions between the
UA string and the values a detector reads back.

Depends on: 0001-0010.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_policy.cc b/chrome/browser/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_policy.cc
